#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:6
msgid "asyncio and free-threaded Python"
msgstr "异步自由线程的 Python"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:8
msgid ""
"asyncio uses an event loop as a scheduler to enable highly efficient "
"concurrency by switching between tasks to allow non-blocking I/O operations."
" This results in better performance for I/O-bound use cases. It also allows "
"off-loading CPU-bound work to a thread or process pool, but that is still "
"limited by the :term:`global interpreter lock` in CPython."
msgstr ""
"asyncio "
"使用事件循环作为调度器，通过在任务之间切换以允许非阻塞输入/输出操作，从而实现高效的并发。这使得它在输入/输出范围用例中具有更好的性能。它还允许将 "
"CPU 密集型工作卸载到线程或进程池中，但这仍然受到 CPython 中 :term:`全局解释器锁 <global interpreter "
"lock>` 的限制。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:15
msgid ""
"However, in :ref:`free-threaded Python <freethreading-python-howto>`, the "
"GIL is disabled and Python can run true multi-threaded code. This means that"
" asyncio can now take advantage of multiple CPU cores without the "
"limitations imposed by the GIL."
msgstr ""
"然而，在 :ref:`自由线程 Python <freethreading-python-howto>` 中，全局解释器锁被禁用，Python "
"可以运行真正的多线程代码。这意味着 asyncio 现在可以利用多个 CPU 核心，而不受全局解释器锁的限制。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:20
msgid ""
"Since Python 3.14, asyncio has first-class support for free-threaded Python,"
" and the implementation of asyncio is safe to use in a multi-threaded "
"environment."
msgstr "从Python 3.14开始，asyncio对自由线程Python提供了一流的支持，并且asyncio的实现可以在多线程环境中安全使用。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:24
msgid ""
"A single event loop on one core can handle many connections concurrently, "
"but the Python code that runs to handle each one still executes serially. "
"Once requests involve a non-trivial amount of per-request computation, that "
"handling becomes the bottleneck, and a single core can no longer keep up. "
"Combining asyncio with threads is most useful here: by running an event loop"
" per thread, the handling of different requests can run in parallel across "
"multiple CPU cores. It is also useful when you need to run blocking or CPU-"
"bound code from an asyncio application."
msgstr ""
"单个核心上的单个事件循环可以并发处理许多连接，但是用于处理每个连接的 Python "
"代码仍然串行执行。一旦请求涉及大量的每个请求计算，该处理就会成为瓶颈，单个核心就无法跟上。在这里，将 asyncio "
"与线程结合使用最为有用：通过每个线程运行一个事件循环，不同请求的处理可以在多个 CPU 核心上并行运行。当你需要从 asyncio 应用程序运行阻塞或 "
"CPU 密集型代码时，它也很有用。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:37
msgid ""
"`Scaling asyncio on Free-Threaded Python "
"<https://labs.quansight.org/blog/scaling-asyncio-on-free-threaded-"
"python>`__, a blog post by Kumar Aditya which explains the internal changes "
"that make asyncio safe and efficient under free-threaded Python, together "
"with benchmarks of the resulting improvements."
msgstr ""
"`在自由线程 Python 上扩展 asyncio <https://labs.quansight.org/blog/scaling-asyncio-"
"on-free-threaded-python>`__，Kumar Aditya 撰写的博客文章，解释了为使 asyncio 在自由线程 Python "
"下安全且高效所做的内部变更，并附有相应改进效果的基准测试数据。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:45
msgid "Thread safety considerations"
msgstr "线程安全注意事项"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:47
msgid ""
"While asyncio is designed to be thread-safe in a free-threaded Python "
"environment, there are still some considerations to keep in mind when using "
"asyncio with threads:"
msgstr "虽然asyncio被设计为在自由线程Python环境中是线程安全的，但在将asyncio与线程一起使用时，仍有一些注意事项需要记住："

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:51
msgid ""
"**Event loop**: Each thread should have its own event loop which should not "
"be shared across threads. This ensures that the event loop can manage its "
"own tasks and callbacks without interference from other threads."
msgstr ""
"**事件循环**：每个线程都应该有自己的事件循环，不应该在线程之间共享。这可以确保事件循环可以管理自己的任务和回调函数，而不会受到其他线程的干扰。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:56
msgid ""
"**Task management**: Tasks and futures created in one thread should not be "
"awaited or manipulated from another thread."
msgstr "**任务管理**：在一个线程中创建的任务和未来不应等待或从另一个线程进行操作。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:59
msgid ""
"**Thread-safe APIs**: When interacting with asyncio from multiple threads, "
"it's important to use thread-safe APIs provided by asyncio, such as "
":func:`asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe` for submitting coroutines to an "
"event loop from another thread. If you need to call a callback from a "
"different thread, you can use :meth:`loop.call_soon_threadsafe` to schedule "
"it safely."
msgstr ""
"**线程安全 API**：当从多个线程与 asyncio 交互时，使用 asyncio 提供的线程安全 API 非常重要，例如 "
":func:`asyncio.run_coroutine_threadsafe` "
"用于从另一个线程向事件循环提交协程。如果你需要从不同的线程调用回调函数，你可以使用 :meth:`loop.call_soon_threadsafe` "
"来安全地调度它。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:66
msgid ""
"**Synchronization**: The synchronization primitives provided by asyncio "
"(like :class:`asyncio.Lock` and :class:`asyncio.Event`) are not designed to "
"be used across threads. If you need to synchronize between threads, you "
"should use the synchronization primitives from the :mod:`threading` module "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"**同步**：asyncio 提供的同步原语（如 :class:`asyncio.Lock` 和 "
":class:`asyncio.Event`）并非设计为跨线程使用。如果需要在线程之间同步，你应该改用 :mod:`threading` "
"模块中的同步原语。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:74
msgid "Using asyncio with threads"
msgstr "在线程中使用asyncio"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:76
msgid ""
"asyncio supports running one event loop per thread, which allows you to take"
" advantage of multiple CPU cores in a free-threaded Python environment. Each"
" thread can run its own event loop, and tasks can be scheduled on those "
"loops independently."
msgstr ""
"asyncio 支持每个线程运行一个事件循环，这允许你在自由线程 Python 环境中利用多个 CPU "
"核心。每个线程都可以运行自己的事件循环，任务可以在这些循环上独立调度。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:81
msgid "Here's an example of how to use asyncio with threads::"
msgstr "下面是如何在线程中使用异步的示例::"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:83
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"async def worker(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} starting\")\n"
"    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} done\")\n"
"\n"
"def run_loop(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    asyncio.run(worker(name))\n"
"\n"
"threads = [\n"
"    threading.Thread(target=run_loop, args=(f\"T{i}\",))\n"
"    for i in range(4)\n"
"]\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.start()\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.join()"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"async def worker(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} starting\")\n"
"    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n"
"    print(f\"Worker {name} done\")\n"
"\n"
"def run_loop(name: str) -> None:\n"
"    asyncio.run(worker(name))\n"
"\n"
"threads = [\n"
"    threading.Thread(target=run_loop, args=(f\"T{i}\",))\n"
"    for i in range(4)\n"
"]\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.start()\n"
"for t in threads:\n"
"    t.join()"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:103
msgid ""
"In this example, each thread creates its own event loop with "
":func:`asyncio.run` and runs a coroutine on it. The threads execute "
"concurrently, and in a free-threaded build they can run on separate CPU "
"cores in parallel."
msgstr ""
"在这个例子中，每个线程都使用 :func:`asyncio.run` "
"创建自己的事件循环，并在其上运行一个协程。这些线程并发执行，并且在自由线程构建版本中，它们可以并行运行在不同的 CPU 核心上。"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:110
msgid "Producer/consumer across threads"
msgstr "跨线程的生产者/使用者"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:112
msgid ""
"When a regular (non-asyncio) thread needs to hand work to an asyncio event "
"loop running in another thread, use a thread-safe primitive such as "
":class:`queue.Queue` rather than :class:`asyncio.Queue`, which is only safe "
"within a single event loop.::"
msgstr ""
"当一个常规 (非 asyncio) 线程需要将工作交给在另一个线程中运行的 asyncio 事件循环时，请使用例如 "
":class:`queue.Queue` 这样的线程安全原语，而不是 :class:`asyncio.Queue`，后者仅在单个事件循环内是安全的。::"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:117
msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import queue\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"def producer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    for i in range(5):\n"
"        print(f\"Producing {i}\")\n"
"        q.put(i)\n"
"    q.shutdown()\n"
"\n"
"async def consumer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    while True:\n"
"        try:\n"
"            item = q.get_nowait()\n"
"        except queue.Empty:\n"
"            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n"
"            continue\n"
"        except queue.ShutDown:\n"
"            break\n"
"        print(f\"Consumed {item}\")\n"
"        await asyncio.sleep(item)\n"
"\n"
"q: queue.Queue[int] = queue.Queue()\n"
"consumer_thread = threading.Thread(\n"
"    target=lambda: asyncio.run(consumer(q))\n"
")\n"
"consumer_thread.start()\n"
"producer(q)\n"
"consumer_thread.join()"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import queue\n"
"import threading\n"
"\n"
"def producer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    for i in range(5):\n"
"        print(f\"Producing {i}\")\n"
"        q.put(i)\n"
"    q.shutdown()\n"
"\n"
"async def consumer(q: queue.Queue[int]) -> None:\n"
"    while True:\n"
"        try:\n"
"            item = q.get_nowait()\n"
"        except queue.Empty:\n"
"            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n"
"            continue\n"
"        except queue.ShutDown:\n"
"            break\n"
"        print(f\"Consumed {item}\")\n"
"        await asyncio.sleep(item)\n"
"\n"
"q: queue.Queue[int] = queue.Queue()\n"
"consumer_thread = threading.Thread(\n"
"    target=lambda: asyncio.run(consumer(q))\n"
")\n"
"consumer_thread.start()\n"
"producer(q)\n"
"consumer_thread.join()"

#: ../../library/asyncio-threading.rst:147
msgid ""
"The producer runs on the main thread while the consumer runs inside an event"
" loop on its own thread, yet they communicate safely through "
"``queue.Queue``. When the queue is empty the consumer sleeps briefly and "
"tries again. When the producer is done it calls "
":meth:`~queue.Queue.shutdown`, which causes subsequent "
":meth:`~queue.Queue.get_nowait` calls to raise :exc:`queue.ShutDown` so the "
"consumer can exit cleanly."
msgstr ""
"生产者在主线程上运行，而使用者在它自己的线程内的事件循环中运行，然而它们通过 ``queue.Queue`` "
"安全地进行通信。当队列为空时，使用者会短暂休眠并重试。当生产者完成时，它会调用 "
":meth:`~queue.Queue.shutdown`，这会导致后续对 :meth:`~queue.Queue.get_nowait` 的调用引发 "
":exc:`queue.ShutDown`，以便使用者可以干净地退出。"
